can pose no threat to us.

64
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:11,250
That's right.

65
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:13,960
I suppose that's a relief.

66
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:18,473
There is still more research to be
done if we are to understand him fully.

67
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:20,540
See those?

68
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:24,597
Those pictures were taken in the cave
where we originally found San Viento.

69
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:26,033
Inspect them carefully.

70
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:28,780
The horns!

71
00:05:28,940 --> 00:05:31,234
They all have different types of horns!

72
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:34,357
So if the one on the bottom
is supposed to be San Viento?

73
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:35,852
then who are the others?

74
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:37,720
According to von Stroheim,

75
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:40,977
the Germans have uncovered another
pillar at an undisclosed location?

76
00:05:41,060 --> 00:05:42,817
somewhere on the European continent.

77
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:43,777
Is that true?

78
00:05:43,860 --> 00:05:46,880
Their faces are stacked
vertically in this picture.

79
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,397
Speaking historically,

80
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:52,937
I would theorize that this indicates
status or rank among the three Pillar Men.

81
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:54,785
Jojo and I are headed to Rome.

82
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:57,077
Von Stroheim told him
that we must go there

83
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:59,748
in order to find the
person who can help us.

84
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:06,100
And it turns out that person is none
other than the grandson of Will A.

85
00:06:06,260 --> 00:06:08,140
Zeppeli, Caesar Zeppeli!

86
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:11,000
Tell me, where might you be from?

87
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:12,817
Would you like me to take a picture?

88
00:06:12,900 --> 00:06:14,797
Perhaps one of you in the fountain?

89
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:15,710
Huh?

90
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:21,537
Boy, the birds in this
country sure are friendly.

91
00:06:21,620 --> 00:06:25,326
They seem much smarter than the
men here, too, don't you think?

92
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:26,860
Knock it off, Jojo.

93
00:06:27,140 --> 00:06:28,937
We didn't come all this way for nothing.

94
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:31,138
The two of you better start talking.

95
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:32,230
Mr.

96
00:06:32,313 --> 00:06:35,120
Speedwagon, I'm sorry, but not a chance.

97
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:39,380
My grandfather died
tragically 50 years ago.

98
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:45,200
My father then took up his torch
and spent his life hunting the mask.

99
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:49,877
We Italians have the strongest familial
bonds of any culture in the world.

100
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:52,240
We are very proud of that tradition.

101
00:06:52,540 --> 00:06:53,920
It is everything to us.

102
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:56,853
That's something he'll never understand.

103
00:06:56,940 --> 00:07:01,477
In fact, you told me he didn't know about
his own grandfather until just recently.

104
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:03,300
A true man knows his history.

105
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:05,737
Tell me this true man is
your host family this dumb.

106
00:07:05,820 --> 00:07:07,232
That's not fair, Caesar.

107
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:11,322
Jojo didn't know anything because
I kept it all a secret from him.

108
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,260
I don't think that's any excuse.

109
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:16,897
I heard about Straizo,

110
00:07:16,980 --> 00:07:20,437
and I was impressed to find out that
he fought one of the Pillar Men.

111
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:24,797
But I wanted to see for myself how
tough he was, so I waited at the hotel.

112
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:29,680
And I'm disappointed to say that his
Hamon skills leave much to be desired.

113
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:31,760
His Hamon is weak.

114
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:32,730
It's worthless.

115
00:07:32,813 --> 00:07:36,940
His defeat of the Pillar Man
was nothing but blind luck!

116
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:40,900
I won't be forced to
work with this imbecile!

117
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:43,117
Caesar, just relax for a moment.

118
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,612
Jojo is still trading...

119
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:48,480
We're done with the niceties here.

120
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:53,395
I'm going to have to settle
this with a good thrashing.

121
00:07:53,700 --> 00:07:58,260
Hamon as weak as yours couldn't pluck
the petals off this delicate flower.

122
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:01,150
Oh, yeah?

123
00:08:01,233 --> 00:08:04,121
Well, you couldn't even
beat one of those pigeons!

124
