Actually, the truth is...

201
00:13:06,100 --> 00:13:10,220
I'll be going home next week so we
can finally get married. Really?

202
00:13:10,660 --> 00:13:11,520
Mamma mia!

203
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:13,397
Congratulations, Mark!

204
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:15,937
I was his wingman when he
picked her up, you know.

205
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:17,079
He was so nervous.

206
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:18,870
Heartwarming.

207
00:13:18,953 --> 00:13:20,817
Please don't get us all killed here.

208
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:24,277
And please stop cuddling with
the wheel if you don't mind.

209
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:28,820
I wanted to ask you, Jojo, do
you have a girlfriend back home?

210
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:32,880
I'll take that as a no, but
you're such a great catch.

211
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:35,338
Why doesn't anyone want to date you?

212
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:38,819
Perhaps they're all too
busy washing their hair, eh?

213
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:42,829
Where does this pompous ass get
off talking to me like that?

214
00:13:43,080 --> 00:13:47,760
Once I develop my own killer technique,
I'll show him a thing or two, or three.

215
00:13:53,940 --> 00:13:55,857
Look, there's something on his head!

216
00:13:55,940 --> 00:13:58,058
I don't think that was there before!

217
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:00,260
Calm down.

218
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:03,577
They're just rocks as long as
they're under those UV lights.

219
00:14:03,660 --> 00:14:04,760
No need to worry.

220
00:14:05,180 --> 00:14:07,340
Now get a closer look! Yes, sir!

221
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:11,760
The death of Von Strauheim's team
is an important lesson to us all.

222
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:14,300
Once we cut this pillar out,

223
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:18,616
we'll have to seal it so that it will
never see the light of day again.

224
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:21,440
I can't tell what that dark spot is.

225
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:23,857
It looks like a hole, but
it might just be a shadow.

226
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:25,280
Get a closer look.

227
00:14:29,460 --> 00:14:31,340
Do you hear that?

228
00:14:34,640 --> 00:14:35,540
His horn!

229
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:37,465
He's supposed to be petrified!

230
00:14:38,740 --> 00:14:40,280
He's making up!

231
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:45,080
Quickly, bring out more UV
lamps! Yes, sir! Schnell!

232
00:14:53,500 --> 00:14:55,220
This can't be happening!

233
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:58,972
He's blocking out the lights
with the blood of my own man!

234
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:20,480
I see the world has undergone
significant changes during my slumber.

235
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:24,132
These insignificant inventions
must be quite popular here.

236
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:25,301
What did he say?

237
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:29,740
I said your pitiful illuminations
are no match against my power!

238
00:15:34,340 --> 00:15:35,780
My hands!

239
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:38,520
We're stuck together!

240
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:03,740
Mama, now is the time.

241
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:05,660
Awaken, my masters!

242
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:20,017
Somehow this doesn't surprise me.

243
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:23,747
The famous mouth of truth was a
secret entrance all this time.

244
00:16:29,080 --> 00:16:31,877
You can really feel the
chill of the dead here.

245
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:35,797
Caesar, what sort of effects has your
Hormone had on the sleeping pillar?

246
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:38,497
Men hormone is only useful on the living.

247
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:39,797
No reason to waste.

248
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:41,233
as my power's on stone.

249
00:16:41,380 --> 00:16:44,027
We can't learn anything
if they're not alive.

250
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:49,420
I'm surprised you Germans don't have
more than zero guards down here.

251
00:16:49,580 --> 00:16:51,340
It's a little quiet. Hello!

252
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:53,700
Stop being foolish, Jojo.

253
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:55,680
Wait, something's wrong.

254
00:16:55,980 --> 00:16:58,897
He's right, there should be guards
posted all around this place.

255
00:16:58,980 --> 00:16:59,810
Really?

256
00:17:03,260 --> 00:17:05,977
Why didn't anyone tell me
there were bats in here?

257
00:17:06,060 --> 00:17:07,957
Gross, I stepped in bat tongue!

258
00:17:08,040 --> 00:17:10,320
And I just cleaned these.

259
00:17:16,380 --> 00:17:17,817
Wait, those are...

260
00:17:17,900 --> 00:17:19,724
They're husks of dead soldiers.

261
00:17:20,320 --> 00:17:22,520
What the hell happened to them?

262
00:17:23,080 --> 00:17:24,080
They're all dead!

263
00:17:25,140 --> 00:17:26,380
Stop where you are!

264
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:28,377
Whoever did this could still be here!

265
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:30,284
We don't know what's out there!

266
00:17:32,520 --> 00:17:33,600
What is that?

267
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:34,818
I can't believe it!

268
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:35,860
They're alive!

269
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:37,037
Run the way, Mark!

270
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:37,950
Mark!

271
00:17:38,033 --> 00:17:38,863
Get out of there now!

272
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:40,330
No!

273
00:17:50,300 --> 00:17:51,130
Mark!

274
00:17:57,300 --> 00:17:58,220
Mark, no!

275
00:17:59,340 --> 00:18:00,820
Ceaser! Ceaser!

276
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:02,336
What have they done?

277
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:07,037
They just walked right through your
friend like he wasn't even there!

278
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:09,097
The Pillar Men have
awoken with such massive

279
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:11,533
power that we barely even exist to them!

280
00:18:11,620 --> 00:18:15,855
We may as well be nothing more than
a colony of ants beneath their feet!

281
00:18:20,120 --> 00:18:22,660
It appears to be night outside, Wamu.

282
00:18:22,860 --> 00:18:24,448
That is correct, Lord Kars.

283
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:26,404
And what shall be your bidding?

284
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:27,690
Easy.

285
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:31,400
We will be searching for the
whereabouts of the Red Stone of Asia.

286
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:35,637
The stone is the last piece we
need in order to complete the mask.

287
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:38,160
Then, we will unleash its power.

288
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:40,200
Of course, Master ACDC.

289
00:18:40,580 --> 00:18:44,757
However, the human world has changed
much over the years that we slumbered.

290
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:48,428
Long ago, it was the Emperor of
Rome who possessed the stone.

291
00:18:49,260 --> 00:18:52,025
Unfortunately, I am
certain that age has ended.

292
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:57,140
Well then, we simply need to find where
it is the stone currently calls home.

293
00:18:57,680 --> 00:19:01,100
They say the Emperor cherished
the stone above all things.

294
00:19:01,600 --> 00:19:05,129
I believe that the humans of
today still tell stories of it.

295
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:08,177
I shall retrieve the
stone for you, my master.

296
00:19:08,260 --> 00:19:09,577
There's time, Wamuu.

297
00:19:09,660 --> 00:19:10,895
For the moment, then.

298
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:15,706
Let us go outside and observe the changes
that have occurred in the human world.

299
00:19:29,660 --> 00:19:30,490
Wamuu!

300
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:32,480
Explain your insolence!

301
00:19:32,700 --> 00:19:34,060
Stay your hand, ACDC.

302
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:37,980
I apologize, Lord Kars.

303
00:19:38,620 --> 00:19:39,620
Of course.

304
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:43,417
It had slipped my mind that
you possess a reflexive attack

305
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:47,382
against anyone who dares to walk
across the depths of your shadow.

306
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:49,977
It has been 2,000 years, after all.

307
00:19:50,060 --> 00:19:51,437
I have offended you, my lord.

308
00:19:51,520 --> 00:19:54,340
I will accept whatever
punishment you see fit.

309
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:57,860
I simply cannot accept your apology.

310
00:19:58,480 --> 00:20:01,797
Your innate fighting spirit is
what makes you a great warrior,

311
00:20:01,880 --> 00:20:03,517
and that is why I trust you.

312
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:07,140
The fault is my own for
treading upon your darkness.

313
00:20:07,300 --> 00:20:09,300
Please forgive my transgression.

314
00:20:09,660 --> 00:20:10,700
You are too kind.

315
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:14,920
Rise, Wamuu.

316
00:20:15,260 --> 00:20:16,240
Yes, Master.

317
00:20:18,540 --> 00:20:19,370
Caesar!

318
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:22,457
Kill me, please! Do it!

319
00:20:22,540 --> 00:20:24,660
You've got to kill me now! I can't.

320
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:26,470
It's...

321
00:20:26,553 --> 00:20:28,860
it's getting so cold. Please, Caesar.

322
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:30,370
I'm...

323
00:20:30,453 --> 00:20:31,283
I'm so scared.

324
00:20:31,366 --> 00:20:35,500
I couldn't feel anything
at first, but now the pain.

325
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:38,871
Please, Caesar, you've got to kill me now.

326
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:42,240
Mark, there's nothing we can do.

327
00:20:42,380 --> 00:20:45,300
I can't do anything to
help this poor bastard.

328
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:47,040
I feel so powerless.

329
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:49,120
I must control myself.

330
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:51,560
I feel like I'm going to explode.

331
00:20:55,020 --> 00:20:56,080
Goodbye, friend.

332
00:20:57,940 --> 00:20:58,770
Caesar.

333
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:02,777
Give out my love, Caesar!

334
00:21:02,860 --> 00:21:03,737
I

335
00:21:03,820 --> 00:21:10,820
promise.

336
00:21:16,940 --> 00:21:21,917
He was so young.

337
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,957
His whole life ahead of him.

338
00:21:24,040 --> 00:21:26,117
He worked hard for a living.

339
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:28,337
He loved his family dearly.

340
00:21:28,420 --> 00:21:31,420
He loved his girl and his country.

341
00:21:31,740 --> 00:21:33,160
He was a good person.

342
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:35,266
Clean cut, the boy next door.

343
00:21:37,020 --> 00:21:38,420
And they killed him.

344
00:21:38,820 --> 00:21:39,800
Now they die!

345
00:21:40,500 --> 00:21:41,330
Caesar!

346
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:46,020
Don't you dare get in my way, Jojo!

347
00:21:46,500 --> 00:21:49,160
I'm going to enjoy every second of this!

348
00:21:49,580 --> 00:21:50,980
This is personal!

349
00:21:51,220 --> 00:21:53,161
I'll destroy these things myself!

350
00:22:28,420 --> 00:22:30,340
We're spitting for the man.

351
00:22:46,660 --> 00:22:48,737
We're closer to all the land.

352
00:22:48,820 --> 00:22:50,117
We're probably no more.

353
00:22:50,200 --> 00:22:51,960
But in frames of sand.

354
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:56,037
He's got to lose all the time.

355
00:22:56,120 --> 00:22:59,500
I want to face his mind in my head.

356
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:03,217
Next to your deeper fears.

357
00:23:03,300 --> 00:23:06,637
He stands around the five million years.

358
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:10,477
I'll give you round the night.

359
00:23:10,560 --> 00:23:14,697
I'll give you round the night.

360
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:17,800
I'll give you round the night.

361
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:31,420
Now I'm sick and tired
of all this talking.

362
00:23:31,620 --> 00:23:32,620
Explain yourself.

363
00:23:32,780 --> 00:23:33,877
What are you trying to get at?

364
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:35,440
I knew he was spineless.

365
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:36,857
These humans know Homo.

366
00:23:36,940 --> 00:23:38,980
I call that Divine Sandstorm.
